WEBVTT

00:01.175 --> 00:04.136
Passione is an extensive
mafia syndicate.

00:04.720 --> 00:09.220
At the bottom of the totem pole are
groups of six to ten members, like us.

00:10.059 --> 00:12.853
Above us are the capos,
sort of branch heads like Polpo.

00:12.895 --> 00:16.064
Each capo oversees
his own territory of business.

00:16.399 --> 00:17.942
And each team has its focus,

00:18.025 --> 00:21.194
whether it be assassinations,
drugs, or otherwise.

00:21.445 --> 00:23.321
While I may be
a part of the famiglia

00:23.406 --> 00:26.367
I chose to not involve myself with
the other team members and capos.

00:26.826 --> 00:29.537
At the head of the famiglia
is the boss.

00:30.121 --> 00:31.705
The boss has
his trusted right-hand man,

00:31.747 --> 00:33.582
with whom he maintains
exclusive communication,

00:33.666 --> 00:37.795
so we have no means of acquiring
his identity or whereabouts.

00:38.087 --> 00:40.547
Mafiosi in Italy hate attracting
attention to themselves

00:40.631 --> 00:42.633
as it puts them at risk
for assassination.

00:43.050 --> 00:44.760
Even capos will dress in a way

00:44.802 --> 00:47.930
that makes them indistinguishable
from ordinary citizens

00:48.014 --> 00:50.391
and some operate
front businesses as well.

00:50.766 --> 00:52.434
The boss is the most
secretive of all.

00:52.476 --> 00:54.811
He makes sure to never reveal
his true identity to anyone.

00:54.812 --> 00:57.147
Any investigative effort is
immediately uncovered.

00:57.190 --> 01:00.026
I know many
who've tried and failed.

01:00.443 --> 01:01.777
So, Giorno…

01:01.819 --> 01:04.488
If you and I want to ever home in
on our man of mystery,

01:04.614 --> 01:06.532
we have to get him to notice us.

01:07.241 --> 01:09.993
We have to gain the trust and acknowledgment
of someone close to the boss

01:10.077 --> 01:12.329
or we'll never overthrow
the man at the top.

01:12.914 --> 01:16.000
First, we have to improve
our standing.

01:16.125 --> 01:18.127
We'll earn the rank of capo.

01:18.169 --> 01:20.337
Of course, we can't go it alone.

01:20.630 --> 01:22.632
We need a team built on trust…

01:22.632 --> 01:25.551
If we want to take him down,
that's the only way.

01:37.063 --> 01:41.563
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

01:42.401 --> 01:45.862
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

01:47.657 --> 01:52.157
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

01:52.828 --> 01:56.665
<i>But I will never give in</i>

01:56.707 --> 02:01.207
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

02:08.511 --> 02:13.011
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

02:21.565 --> 02:26.065
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

02:27.530 --> 02:32.030
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

02:34.620 --> 02:37.748
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

02:37.832 --> 02:42.332
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

02:43.045 --> 02:47.545
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

02:57.101 --> 03:01.601
EPISODE 05
FIND POLPO'S FORTUNE!

02:57.393 --> 03:02.085
<i>Among Passione's capos,
news of Polpo's death spread like wildfire.</i>

03:02.648 --> 03:05.525
The guys in intelligence say
it might be suicide.

03:05.651 --> 03:07.110
That's just not like him.

03:07.236 --> 03:11.281
That was a maximum security cell.
Nobody'd be able to kill that bastard.

03:11.365 --> 03:13.492
So maybe he betrayed the boss…

03:13.576 --> 03:16.328
You couldn't find a more loyal capo
than Polpo.

03:16.412 --> 03:18.163
There's no frickin' way.

03:18.247 --> 03:19.414
Yeah, but…

03:19.457 --> 03:20.958
- Well, what I'm worried about…
- So what do you think?

03:21.042 --> 03:22.585
Is his replacement.

03:23.836 --> 03:28.336
ROME 10:05 A.M.

03:24.295 --> 03:29.112
I just heard the capos
are fuori di testa.

03:29.216 --> 03:31.259
Apparently,
Polpo committed suicide.

03:31.302 --> 03:32.136
Huh?

03:33.095 --> 03:34.721
Hey, keep your eyes on the road!

03:34.764 --> 03:35.723
I got this.

03:35.765 --> 03:37.641
Suicide? That fat-ass?

03:39.143 --> 03:40.936
I said keep your eyes on the road!

03:41.395 --> 03:42.646
Who knows?

03:43.105 --> 03:44.773
Maybe he was tired of
looking like a slob,

03:44.815 --> 03:47.776
or maybe life in that cell
finally got to him.

03:47.860 --> 03:51.363
Whatever the reason, at least now
we know he was just a big pussy.

03:51.697 --> 03:53.615
He bit down on the peashooter

03:53.657 --> 03:55.492
and painted the walls
with his brains.

03:55.576 --> 03:59.037
You sure he killed himself and
wasn't offed by someone else?

03:59.121 --> 04:00.831
Trust me, it was suicide.

04:00.873 --> 04:02.457
The autopsy guy or whatever
he's called said so.

04:02.541 --> 04:04.709
Any expert worth a damn
can tell the difference

04:04.794 --> 04:06.504
between a suicide case and murder.

04:06.545 --> 04:07.796
Hey, there's a light, dingaling.

04:10.257 --> 04:11.508
All right, it's question time…

04:11.550 --> 04:13.969
You know the rumors
about Polpo's fortune?

04:14.011 --> 04:15.178
Rumors?

04:15.221 --> 04:18.349
I know more about astrophysics
than I do about that damn rumor.

04:18.516 --> 04:20.601
Before Polpo got locked up

04:20.643 --> 04:24.313
he converted some of his cash
into a stash of rubies and gold

04:24.355 --> 04:26.899
or so the rumor says.

04:27.358 --> 04:28.859
Like hidden treasure…

04:29.610 --> 04:30.694
He had so much dough,

04:30.778 --> 04:33.530
it was too much for the bank and
apparently for the famiglia too.

04:33.572 --> 04:38.072
No one had the balls to look for it
while Polpo was alive.

04:38.661 --> 04:42.873
But now the chump's a goner,
so it's anyone's cash.

04:42.957 --> 04:44.750
It's free money.

04:44.834 --> 04:47.670
Supposedly, he hid some
five billion lira.

04:48.671 --> 04:50.255
Five billion?

04:51.340 --> 04:53.383
If I had that kind of moolah,

04:53.509 --> 04:56.011
I'd have a chick on each arm
on my way to Monaco or Japan.

04:56.137 --> 04:59.056
Nah, I'd rather spend my time
working my way up in the famiglia.

04:59.181 --> 05:00.640
Once I buy my way
to the rank of capo,

05:00.683 --> 05:03.477
I'll be savoring some nectar
that you can only dream of.

05:03.894 --> 05:05.854
But where'd the hell
did he hide it…?

05:06.021 --> 05:07.897
Isn't there anyone who knows?

05:08.315 --> 05:11.735
Nope, but here's what I'm thinking…

05:11.986 --> 05:14.363
That tub of lard probably couldn't
crawl his way out of that cell

05:14.405 --> 05:15.697
without a crew of helpers.

05:15.823 --> 05:17.074
You think a guy like that

05:17.158 --> 05:19.201
could hide five billion in loot
all by his lonesome?

05:19.243 --> 05:21.161
He had to have had some help.

05:21.328 --> 05:23.496
Some kind of loyal confidant…

05:23.581 --> 05:27.418
True confidants are
few and far between.

05:27.543 --> 05:29.795
But Polpo liked Bucciarati.

05:29.879 --> 05:33.007
Bucciarati? You mean that teppista
from Napoli, right?

05:33.048 --> 05:36.760
Yeah. If he had anyone hide it,
it'd be him.

05:36.802 --> 05:38.261
And now that Polpo's dead,

05:38.304 --> 05:40.848
Bucciarati must've already
sprung into action…

05:41.015 --> 05:44.435
With five billion lira just there
for the taking, and all.

05:44.518 --> 05:47.521
I'm sure even Bucciarati has
a greedy streak in him.

05:50.483 --> 05:52.067
Hey, Zucchero!

05:54.653 --> 05:57.614
That bastard Zucchero
actually took off!

05:57.698 --> 05:59.324
He really believed all that crap?

05:59.575 --> 06:03.662
But if you're going to tail Bucciarati,
I'd be careful.

06:03.871 --> 06:06.373
Word has it, he and his little helpers
are Stand users.

06:06.540 --> 06:08.166
NAPOLI 11:26 A.M.

06:09.043 --> 06:11.170
Hey, Fugo.

06:11.253 --> 06:13.171
It's freakin' beautiful out there.

06:13.297 --> 06:16.341
One day away from
the books isn't gonna hurt.

06:16.425 --> 06:19.803
- I'm just not into it today.
- Thank you for waiting. Torta alle fragola.

06:21.222 --> 06:22.681
- Listen, Narancia.
- Put it over there.

06:23.432 --> 06:25.225
- You should be commended.
- Si, signore.

06:25.476 --> 06:28.479
It's not easy to ask for
academic guidance

06:28.521 --> 06:31.899
especially when you barely
went to class in grade school.

06:32.191 --> 06:34.902
Yet you still managed to learn
your multiplication tables!

06:35.277 --> 06:37.320
You can do it,
just remember what I taught you.

06:37.446 --> 06:39.322
If anyone can do it, it's you.

06:40.282 --> 06:43.451
Okay, now what's six times five?

06:43.619 --> 06:47.247
Six times five is… six… five…

06:47.915 --> 06:48.665
Thirty?

06:48.749 --> 06:51.835
Bravo… I told you, you could do it!

06:51.961 --> 06:53.963
You're practically half way there!

06:54.046 --> 06:57.340
I get it! Six times five is thirty!
Right!

06:57.633 --> 06:59.843
Hey, what the hell is this?!

06:59.969 --> 07:01.804
What? It's strawberry…

07:01.845 --> 07:04.389
I can see it's strawberry, dumb-ass!

07:04.473 --> 07:08.059
It's not like I'd think it's chocolate
or some cheese cake!

07:08.102 --> 07:09.812
You missed the point!

07:09.895 --> 07:11.521
There are four slices here!

07:11.605 --> 07:13.690
They might as well've said die!

07:14.984 --> 07:16.610
Another hissy fit, Mista?

07:16.652 --> 07:17.736
Ah shut up!

07:17.903 --> 07:21.197
Taking one of the four is bad luck!

07:21.198 --> 07:23.700
Making a selection
from five is okay.

07:23.742 --> 07:26.202
Making a selection
from three is okay.

07:26.245 --> 07:30.040
Choosing anything from a group of
four practically guarantees disaster!

07:30.499 --> 07:33.460
When I was a kid, a neighborhood cat
had four kittens

07:33.502 --> 07:36.129
and one of my friends ended up
adopting one of them.

07:36.297 --> 07:40.509
Well, that cat scratched my friend's eye
clear out of the socket!

07:40.593 --> 07:43.721
Of course, he then beat that kitty
till it was dead and gone.

07:43.846 --> 07:45.848
That's just some
idiotic superstition.

07:46.348 --> 07:47.766
Just take a moment and think…

07:47.850 --> 07:49.643
If the cake disappears
one slice at a time,

07:49.685 --> 07:52.145
eventually, someone's going to be stuck
having to choose one piece from the four.

07:52.187 --> 07:53.229
Exactly!

07:53.522 --> 07:56.775
This is when the restaurant staff should
take the hint and bring out three slices!

07:57.192 --> 07:59.402
The service here sucks!

07:59.486 --> 08:02.572
Ufa… Then don't eat it.

08:04.283 --> 08:06.785
I demand to eat
torta alle fragole!

08:06.869 --> 08:08.245
I did it!

08:08.287 --> 08:09.997
I'm done, Fugo… So?

08:10.831 --> 08:12.666
It's completed? Okay, let's see…

08:14.627 --> 08:15.711
What is this?

08:16.879 --> 08:18.005
Did I get it right?

08:19.840 --> 08:21.424
CRUNCH

08:23.552 --> 08:27.055
Measly little punk shit!
You think you can mess with me?!

08:27.056 --> 08:29.767
How many times
do I have to tell you?!

08:30.017 --> 08:32.769
Pea-brained punk-assed
chowder head!

08:33.687 --> 08:36.189
- Yep, that's it, he's definitely lost it now.
- You just said six times five was thirty!

08:36.231 --> 08:38.483
- Hey, Abbacchio,
- How the hell…

08:38.567 --> 08:41.194
- you gonna eat the rest of that or what?
- do you now come up with that number?!

08:41.945 --> 08:43.446
What'd you call me?

08:43.572 --> 08:46.074
I heard pea-brained punk-assed
chowder head?

08:46.158 --> 08:49.077
You know, talking down to
people isn't very nice.

08:49.161 --> 08:50.162
I'll cut you.

08:50.245 --> 08:53.081
- I swear I'll slice you to pieces, Fugo.
- Dirty bastardo…

08:53.123 --> 08:55.959
Fools, what do you think
you're doing?!

08:56.210 --> 08:58.962
I could hear your tedious bickering
all the way from the front of the building!

08:59.463 --> 09:01.339
Can't you see, you're bothering
the other customers!

09:03.967 --> 09:06.344
I've brought the new associate
we talked about.

09:07.012 --> 09:09.764
Now pay attention.
This is Giorno Giovanna.

09:19.358 --> 09:20.984
I'm Giorno Giovanna.

09:21.568 --> 09:23.194
It's an honor to meet you.

09:26.615 --> 09:28.033
Forgive me, Fugo.

09:28.117 --> 09:29.326
No, I should apologize.

09:29.451 --> 09:30.827
Please forgive me, Narancia.

09:30.911 --> 09:34.831
I promise I'll study hard.
Please keep being my teacher.

09:34.998 --> 09:35.832
Listen, everyone!

09:36.333 --> 09:39.294
I went out of my way to bring him here.
Let's show him some respect!

09:39.336 --> 09:40.211
Mr. Bucciarati.

09:41.004 --> 09:42.046
What is it?

09:42.131 --> 09:43.632
You have a phone call, signore.

09:43.966 --> 09:45.509
Right, thank you.

09:45.968 --> 09:49.638
I expect you all to properly
introduce yourselves! Capito?

09:49.680 --> 09:51.640
Giorno, I'll be right back.

09:51.807 --> 09:54.935
I'd like you to take some time to get
to know your fellow team members.

09:55.018 --> 09:56.394
Yes, of course.

09:58.772 --> 10:00.523
Giorno, was it?

10:01.525 --> 10:03.693
Don't just stand there,
take a load off.

10:04.194 --> 10:06.321
- Let's have some tea and chat.
- Signore Bucciarati.

10:06.321 --> 10:07.071
- Let's have some tea and chat.
- Grazie.

10:08.240 --> 10:09.366
Bucciarati speaking.

10:13.662 --> 10:14.829
Got it.

10:17.082 --> 10:18.708
Is something the matter?

10:18.751 --> 10:19.376
No.

10:19.376 --> 10:22.962
Bucciarati! Bucciarati,
scusa un attimo?

10:23.088 --> 10:25.840
Oh, Signora Menini, hello.

10:26.091 --> 10:27.634
What can I do for you?

10:27.718 --> 10:32.180
I'd like you to lend me an ear.
Mind if we chat outside?

10:32.598 --> 10:33.682
Of course.

10:38.812 --> 10:40.188
Well, down the hatch.

10:43.192 --> 10:44.818
How old are you?

10:44.902 --> 10:45.903
Fifteen.

10:45.944 --> 10:50.156
Fifteen? Ha, I've even got
two years on ya.

10:50.199 --> 10:51.074
I appreciate it.

10:58.373 --> 10:59.916
What's wrong?

11:00.000 --> 11:02.752
You wait, yet you've already
expressed your gratitude

11:02.795 --> 11:04.797
for the tea I so graciously
poured for you.

11:05.297 --> 11:08.591
You've said your niceties.
It's time to drink up.

11:08.759 --> 11:11.386
Could it be that the tea
is unpleasantly lukewarm?

11:11.553 --> 11:15.557
Maybe he doesn't want to drink it because
he doesn't want to be one of us.

11:15.766 --> 11:17.642
What's going on here now?!

11:17.726 --> 11:19.602
Nothing, everything's fine.

11:19.853 --> 11:23.106
He went to the trouble of preparing
a special cup of tea, just for me.

11:27.110 --> 11:28.611
Holy freakin' shit…

11:29.071 --> 11:30.655
What did you do to his…?

11:35.744 --> 11:38.747
Gross! He actually drank it!

11:39.331 --> 11:42.125
You're really gonna be some fun…
You really drank that stuff?

11:42.209 --> 11:43.877
No, there's no way he drank it!

11:43.961 --> 11:46.129
Hey, how'd you do that?
Where'd you put it?

11:46.171 --> 11:48.882
Hey, tell me the trick.
It's safe with me, please?

11:49.049 --> 11:50.300
Dunno…

11:50.801 --> 11:54.012
I would guess all of you are keeping
your abilities under wraps as well, no?

11:56.223 --> 11:58.600
<i>So this stronzo's a Stand user…</i>

11:59.393 --> 12:01.311
<i>The liquid in the cup…</i>

12:01.353 --> 12:04.481
<i>was absorbed by my left front tooth</i>

12:04.565 --> 12:07.150
<i>which I transformed into
the ninety-eight-percent-water jellyfish.</i>

12:07.359 --> 12:09.527
- Can you transport matter at will?
- Open your mouth.

12:09.611 --> 12:10.653
There must be some hidden cavity.

12:10.779 --> 12:12.655
- You really drank it?
<i>- I don't know what it is</i>

12:12.698 --> 12:14.366
- Is that like your favorite drink?
<i>- but there's something about Giorno Giovanna</i>

12:14.449 --> 12:16.576
- I suppose if you tell me your powers,
<i>- that gives him the unique ability</i>

12:16.618 --> 12:18.703
- I could reciprocate.
<i>- to charm almost anyone.</i>

12:18.787 --> 12:21.664
You think before you act.
I like that.

12:21.707 --> 12:23.667
Does Bucciarati know?

12:23.709 --> 12:24.835
You could say that.

12:25.210 --> 12:29.710
<i>We're not exactly a cohesive team,
but we have to act.</i>

12:31.550 --> 12:33.051
<i>Indecision is a luxury
we can't afford.</i>

12:33.635 --> 12:36.346
Listen, men, it's time to get serious.
We're heading out.

12:36.430 --> 12:37.722
Huh? Where to?

12:37.931 --> 12:40.141
Follow me and you'll find out.
Come on.

12:45.439 --> 12:46.857
Bucciarati! Ciao?

12:46.899 --> 12:48.108
Oh, Signore Bucciarati!

12:48.317 --> 12:49.359
Hey, Bucciarati.

12:49.484 --> 12:51.777
Come back to our store soon!

12:51.820 --> 12:53.112
Indeed I will, signore!

12:53.238 --> 12:54.906
Hey, so what about a car then?

12:54.990 --> 12:56.116
I borrowed one.

12:56.283 --> 12:57.575
- Thanks to a certain someone
<i>- Just as I suspected,</i>

12:57.659 --> 12:59.702
- who had to total our last one.
<i>- people really trust him.</i>

12:59.786 --> 13:01.579
There was no way to avoid that!

13:04.458 --> 13:08.253
<i>Bucciarati, meet my dear friend</i>

13:08.337 --> 13:12.424
<i>Hereon is beating her,
and she is completely distraught.</i>

13:12.507 --> 13:13.382
<i>Right?</i>

13:14.384 --> 13:17.428
<i>Is that so?
Of course you're distraught, signora.</i>

13:17.512 --> 13:19.722
<i>I'll be sure to have
a serious conversation with him.</i>

13:19.806 --> 13:21.140
<i>May I ask what is your son's name?</i>

13:21.558 --> 13:22.934
<i>Grazie, tesoro.</i>

13:23.018 --> 13:25.228
<i>Deep down, he's a good boy</i>

13:25.687 --> 13:28.564
<i>But now, drugs are his…</i>

13:29.066 --> 13:33.403
<i>Bucciarati, this neighborhood has been
my home for the past fifty years.</i>

13:33.737 --> 13:36.990
<i>But now, it's different…
It fills me with worry.</i>

13:37.032 --> 13:39.492
<i>Who would make a boy
do such a thing?</i>

13:39.701 --> 13:42.078
<i>I've never been so scared</i>

13:42.162 --> 13:45.665
<i>You'll keep us safe,
won't you, Bucciarati?</i>

13:45.707 --> 13:49.794
<i>You're one of us,
aren't you, right?</i>

13:50.712 --> 13:53.589
<i>Yes, you can rest easy…</i>

13:54.091 --> 13:55.675
<i>I will find a solution.</i>

14:02.599 --> 14:04.934
So what you meant was
we were going yachting?

14:04.977 --> 14:06.103
That's awesome!

14:06.395 --> 14:08.605
When did you get
a hold of a yacht?

14:08.647 --> 14:09.689
We're going to rent one.

14:09.731 --> 14:10.481
Huh?

14:10.482 --> 14:11.941
Aw, it's just a rental.

14:12.484 --> 14:14.110
So, Bucciarati…

14:14.861 --> 14:18.281
Do me a favor… Whatever you do,
do not rent yacht number four, okay?

14:18.365 --> 14:19.616
We'll sink to our deaths.

14:19.658 --> 14:20.909
Oh, give me a break.

14:21.076 --> 14:23.078
Then it wouldn't be floating
right in front of us, would it?

14:23.120 --> 14:24.121
Shut up!

14:24.287 --> 14:26.205
Then that can be your yacht!

14:29.459 --> 14:31.919
We'd like to rent a yacht.

14:32.045 --> 14:36.466
Prego prego!
Choose whichever one you like best.

14:36.633 --> 14:37.967
Not number four!

14:38.010 --> 14:41.722
Understood.
We'll take the one on the far left.

14:41.888 --> 14:44.807
Certainly signore.
I'll go fetch your keys.

14:45.767 --> 14:48.269
I'm interested in renting
the craft for three days.

14:48.311 --> 14:49.061
How much will that cost me?

14:49.104 --> 14:52.649
From you, Signore Bucciarati,
I could never take money!

14:53.358 --> 14:54.609
Use it as you need to.

14:54.693 --> 14:55.985
Grazie Mille.

14:56.111 --> 14:59.072
Hey, old guy,
get over here and ring me up!

15:23.013 --> 15:25.056
Yep, this is the life.

15:28.685 --> 15:31.312
Hey, Narancia… Hey!

15:32.606 --> 15:33.523
Huh?

15:33.607 --> 15:36.443
Well, uh, about that…

15:36.568 --> 15:39.779
Hey, you bought
a bunch of drinks, right?

15:39.821 --> 15:41.364
Wanna sell me one?

15:41.531 --> 15:44.909
What? Sounds great,
but you never pay up!

15:44.993 --> 15:48.788
What's the difference? Gimme one!
Come on, here!

15:49.039 --> 15:50.373
Why do I bother?

15:50.499 --> 15:52.375
You want a cola or Spa-rite?

15:52.375 --> 15:56.462
I'll take a co— Actually, a Spa-rite.
I can see all the little bubbles.

15:58.340 --> 15:59.007
Here you go.

15:59.007 --> 16:02.260
Thanks.
Here, hold this book a second.

16:04.346 --> 16:06.639
Grazie, and grazie again…

16:14.773 --> 16:17.358
Huh? What the hell?
It just stopped!

16:17.400 --> 16:18.609
Why'd it stop?

16:18.693 --> 16:20.361
I just bought it!

16:20.570 --> 16:23.406
Shit, shit, shit!
Bastard sold me a dud!

16:23.490 --> 16:25.909
Cheap electronics peddling geezer,
you're not gonna get away with this!

16:25.992 --> 16:26.701
Hey!

16:26.701 --> 16:28.994
Bucciarati,
enough of the surprises.

16:29.037 --> 16:32.999
Where are you having
this boat take us?!

16:34.501 --> 16:37.128
Now it's safe.
We're far enough from shore.

16:41.091 --> 16:43.760
Our destination is… Capri.

16:43.844 --> 16:45.053
Capri?

16:45.095 --> 16:47.430
I take it we're not going for
the amazing views…

16:47.556 --> 16:48.098
Yeah.

16:48.098 --> 16:51.267
So then,
what's the point of all this?

16:51.434 --> 16:54.979
Today, Polpo, the capo,
took his own life.

16:55.188 --> 16:57.607
What? He killed himself?! Polpo?

16:57.691 --> 16:58.525
You're shitting me!

16:58.608 --> 16:59.358
Why?

16:59.442 --> 17:01.777
The why doesn't matter.

17:01.903 --> 17:05.448
Polpo was a capo
who constantly courted death.

17:05.740 --> 17:09.785
But what's all that got to do
with Capri?

17:09.870 --> 17:12.956
Polpo was hiding
a vast personal fortune.

17:13.123 --> 17:14.499
A fortune worth…

17:14.583 --> 17:16.084
ten billion lira!

17:17.169 --> 17:19.004
T-Ten billion?

17:19.087 --> 17:21.589
I'm the only one who knows
the location.

17:21.715 --> 17:24.467
He ordered me to hide the treasure.

17:24.593 --> 17:26.803
That ten billion lira belongs
in our hands now!

17:26.928 --> 17:30.014
With that kind of capital,
we will achieve the rank of capo!

17:30.599 --> 17:32.183
Hell yeah!

17:33.768 --> 17:36.479
<i>There's no question,
he's destined for the top.</i>

17:36.521 --> 17:38.981
<i>I predicted it.
He will become a capo!</i>

17:39.065 --> 17:40.524
<i>This is an opportunity</i>

17:40.609 --> 17:44.029
<i>born of pure perseverance
and hard work.</i>

17:44.112 --> 17:45.321
<i>I wouldn't expect less.</i>

17:45.405 --> 17:46.656
<i>Well, whaddya know…</i>

17:46.740 --> 17:49.409
<i>Things just got
a whole lot more interesting.</i>

17:49.534 --> 17:50.451
Where is it?

17:50.452 --> 17:53.955
Where'd you stash that kind of
treasure on Capri, Bucciarati?

17:54.039 --> 17:55.665
I'm not yet at liberty to say.

17:55.790 --> 17:57.583
Rumors about its whereabouts
have been swirling

17:57.626 --> 17:59.502
among members of the famiglia
for a while.

17:59.586 --> 18:03.548
Until we can secure the goods,
we remain on high alert.

18:04.966 --> 18:06.801
B-Bucciarati!

18:06.885 --> 18:08.386
Hey! Something strange
is happening!

18:08.762 --> 18:10.305
Say something, Narancia.

18:13.308 --> 18:14.058
Narancia!

18:14.142 --> 18:16.102
Hey, quit messing around.

18:17.270 --> 18:19.522
Hey, guys, come here quick!

18:21.441 --> 18:23.025
One lone shoe…

18:23.068 --> 18:24.360
Give me that, Giorno!

18:24.653 --> 18:26.655
Nothing is making any sense…

18:26.696 --> 18:29.031
I don't get it…
Where could he've gone?

18:29.658 --> 18:31.701
None of you saw anything?

18:31.701 --> 18:33.035
From what I could see,

18:33.078 --> 18:37.040
it looked as if Narancia
was pulled into this box.

18:37.165 --> 18:38.499
What?

18:38.541 --> 18:40.334
That's impossible!

18:40.377 --> 18:43.630
He couldn't have plopped
straight into the ocean, could he?

18:43.713 --> 18:45.589
Narancia, where are you?

18:45.715 --> 18:49.218
Hey, Narancia!
If this is all some big joke… Hup!

18:49.261 --> 18:51.471
Just hurry up and say something!

18:52.681 --> 18:55.058
- Narancia, where are you?
- Narancia! Answer us!

18:56.101 --> 18:57.060
Mista?

18:58.436 --> 19:00.354
What are you doing, Mista?

19:01.439 --> 19:02.356
Mista?

19:03.191 --> 19:05.193
Where are you, Mista?

19:05.235 --> 19:06.569
There's no way…

19:07.529 --> 19:08.696
Come on, Mista!

19:09.281 --> 19:10.991
Don't tell me you're in on this no—

19:13.285 --> 19:14.077
Fugo?

19:16.037 --> 19:17.163
Hey, Fugo!

19:17.872 --> 19:18.747
What?

19:18.790 --> 19:19.707
Could this be…?

19:19.791 --> 19:22.960
Abbacchio, Giorno,
I need you to stick together!

19:23.003 --> 19:24.462
We're under attack!

19:24.921 --> 19:28.090
There's no question whatsoever,
we've got a stowaway!

19:28.133 --> 19:29.425
This is the work of a Stand!

19:29.718 --> 19:31.511
But why all of a sudden here?

19:31.553 --> 19:32.804
The money.

19:33.972 --> 19:37.600
Word got out I know
where the treasure lies

19:37.684 --> 19:39.477
and now they're after it too.

19:39.602 --> 19:41.270
Someone else from the famiglia.

19:42.439 --> 19:46.939
You think someone's been stalking us
all the way from the docks?

19:47.444 --> 19:48.695
Sure seems like it.

19:48.903 --> 19:51.447
They knew I'd never
let the secret out,

19:51.489 --> 19:53.282
so they probably
got sick of waiting.

19:53.408 --> 19:55.284
Our pursuer will try to off
every one of you except yours truly.

19:55.327 --> 19:57.203
After which,
he will try to get me to confess.

19:57.287 --> 19:59.455
Out here, we're trapped like rats,

19:59.497 --> 20:01.290
and he's in no rush
to speed up the killing.

20:01.583 --> 20:03.418
So you think Narancia
and the others are goners?

20:03.543 --> 20:04.961
That's not what I'm saying.

20:05.003 --> 20:06.713
Remember, ten billion is at stake.

20:06.755 --> 20:09.966
They won't hesitate for a second
to kill one of their own.

20:10.258 --> 20:12.760
Listen, Narancia and
the others are alive.

20:13.595 --> 20:15.430
They're somewhere on this boat.

20:16.056 --> 20:18.808
I don't know whether
they're being held as hostages,

20:18.850 --> 20:20.184
but they're alive.

20:21.311 --> 20:22.812
Giorno Giovanna…

20:22.896 --> 20:27.150
what makes you so sure
about that?

20:28.526 --> 20:32.029
I used my Stand to turn
Narancia's shoe into a fly.

20:32.530 --> 20:35.491
The fly is simply trying
to return to its owner.

20:35.992 --> 20:37.493
If Narancia had been killed,

20:37.577 --> 20:39.996
the fly would not be hovering
and searching as we speak.

20:40.121 --> 20:41.413
Can you locate him?

20:41.456 --> 20:44.459
He's alive… He's alive, but…

20:44.876 --> 20:47.920
It's not descending into
the lower cabin or locker.

20:47.962 --> 20:49.922
It keeps going…

20:50.298 --> 20:54.010
It keeps searching for Narancia
over there.

20:54.094 --> 20:56.596
What in god's name
is this guy's power?

20:56.638 --> 20:58.389
Stop talking for a moment
and listen.

20:58.598 --> 21:02.101
Narancia's somewhere over there
by the cabin entrance.

21:02.185 --> 21:03.603
I'm one hundred percent sure.

21:03.812 --> 21:04.938
But for some reason,

21:04.979 --> 21:07.815
it can't pinpoint his location,
so it's disoriented.

21:08.316 --> 21:11.694
We should consider Narancia's location
as the enemy's location.

21:12.195 --> 21:16.695
In other words, our enemy isn't simply
hiding in the shadows of the hull.

21:18.076 --> 21:19.202
Ah, va bene.

21:19.619 --> 21:22.330
Unless we decipher
the enemy's abilities,

21:22.414 --> 21:24.874
one misstep could
cost us our lives.

21:24.958 --> 21:25.917
Yes.

21:26.167 --> 21:30.171
He may be able to attack in hiding,
but that's also a weakness.

21:30.255 --> 21:33.258
Once we figure out how his Stand works,
we can take him down.

21:34.509 --> 21:37.845
Abbacchio, your Stand…

21:38.388 --> 21:41.641
might just be
our perfect secret weapon.

21:42.350 --> 21:43.392
Secret weapon?

21:43.977 --> 21:46.980
You have the ability
to solve this mystery?

21:50.024 --> 21:50.774
Perhaps…

21:51.443 --> 21:52.902
Hey, Abbacchio!

21:52.944 --> 21:57.198
I should hope a personal hang-up
isn't getting in the way of our survival!

21:57.240 --> 21:58.532
Personal hang-up, huh?

21:58.658 --> 21:59.784
No.

21:59.868 --> 22:02.287
I put a value on my safety.

22:02.370 --> 22:04.914
I can't just reveal my Stand

22:04.914 --> 22:08.500
in the presence of a complete stranger
who has zero loyalty to me.

22:09.127 --> 22:10.336
Bucciarati…

22:10.420 --> 22:14.048
I don't know why you place
so much trust in this guy.

22:14.090 --> 22:17.218
In my eyes,
he's no associate of mine.

22:17.552 --> 22:19.095
If we don't crack this mystery,

22:19.137 --> 22:20.596
this enemy Stand will kill
each and every one of us!

22:20.680 --> 22:25.180
That's just
this outsider kid's guess.

22:25.268 --> 22:28.604
That's just his cowardice talking.
He's seen nothing.

22:28.730 --> 22:29.564
Abbacchio!

22:29.606 --> 22:33.735
That bastard's just hiding
somewhere down below.

22:33.776 --> 22:37.196
I'll weed him out
and give him his due.

22:37.238 --> 22:40.449
If we rush in without knowing how
his Stand works, he'll kill us for—

22:40.533 --> 22:41.617
Why don't you shut up?!

22:43.536 --> 22:46.121
Piece of shit kid…

22:49.000 --> 22:51.669
I refuse to give up on my dream.

22:51.753 --> 22:53.463
What the hell
are you talking about?

22:55.632 --> 22:57.592
Hey, you can crack
this mystery, right?

22:58.092 --> 22:59.009
Don't let me down now!

22:59.093 --> 22:59.968
Giorno!

23:00.053 --> 23:01.304
What in the world are you…?

23:06.976 --> 23:10.145
ROAR

23:08.728 --> 23:10.146
G-Giorno!

23:13.775 --> 23:15.318
That's where the enemy's hiding!

23:15.527 --> 23:16.277
Merda!

23:16.277 --> 23:17.820
Giorno's in trouble!

23:18.947 --> 23:19.906
Abbacchio…

23:20.490 --> 23:24.990
Giorno Giovanna…
You're one folle idiot a.

23:25.411 --> 23:27.204
You really want to prove yourself…

23:31.000 --> 23:33.002
That boy's just not right
in the head.

23:37.882 --> 23:41.635
EPISODE 06
MOODY JAZZ'S COUNTERATTACK
